# =============================================================================
# attr(5) — Extended Attributes Configuration
# =============================================================================
# This template configures system-wide extended attribute behavior.
#
# IMPORTANT: Most extended attribute limits are imposed by the VFS and the
# specific filesystem driver. They are NOT dynamically configurable at runtime
# via this file. This file serves primarily as:
#   1. A documentation anchor for administrators.
#   2. A place to record recommended mount options (hints, not enforced).
#   3. A placeholder for filesystem-specific documentation limits.
#
# The kernel's actual limits are defined in:
#   - fs/xattr.c (VFS xattr implementation)
#   - Individual filesystem drivers (ext4, xfs, btrfs, etc.)
#
# Reference: attr(5) man page, Linux VFS documentation.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User-space hints for filesystem mount options
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: List of mount options recommended to enable extended attributes
# support for user attributes (e.g., 'user_xattr' for ext2/ext3/ext4).
# Note: These are NOT enforced by the kernel. They serve as guidance for
# system administrators setting up filesystems with xattr support.
#
# Schema Field: xattr_mount_opts (list of strings)
# Default: ['user_xattr']
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{% for opt in (xattr_mount_opts | default(['user_xattr'])) %}
# Recommended mount option: {{ opt }}
{% endfor %}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VFS-imposed limit: maximum length of attribute name
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: Maximum length (in bytes) of an attribute name, as imposed by
# the VFS. This is a fixed kernel constant and CANNOT be changed via config.
# It is documented here for reference.
#
# Schema Field: max_attr_name_len (integer)
# Default: 255
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# max_attr_name_len = {{ (max_attr_name_len | default(255)) }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VFS-imposed limit: maximum size of attribute value
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: Maximum size (in bytes) of a single attribute value, as imposed
# by the VFS. This is a fixed kernel constant and CANNOT be changed via config.
# It is documented here for reference.
#
# Schema Field: max_attr_value_len (integer)
# Default: 65536
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# max_attr_value_len = {{ (max_attr_value_len | default(65536)) }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VFS-imposed limit: maximum total size of listxattr result
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: Maximum total size (in bytes) of the list returned by
# listxattr(2). This is a fixed kernel constant and CANNOT be changed via config.
# It is documented here for reference.
#
# Schema Field: max_listxattr_result_len (integer)
# Default: 65536
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# max_listxattr_result_len = {{ (max_listxattr_result_len | default(65536)) }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Filesystem-specific extended attribute limits
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: List of filesystem-specific limits. These are for DOCUMENTATION
# purposes only. Each item is a dict with keys: 'fs' (filesystem name) and
# 'max_total_bytes_per_file' (limit in bytes).
#
# Schema Field: fs_limits (list of dicts)
# Default: []
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{% for limit_entry in (fs_limits | default([])) %}
# Filesystem: {{ limit_entry['fs'] | default('unknown') }}
# Max total extended attributes space per file: {{ limit_entry['max_total_bytes_per_file'] | default(0) }} bytes
# Typically constrained by filesystem block/node size
{% endfor %}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extended attribute namespace rules (documentation only)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Attribute names MUST be in the form: namespace.attribute
# Allowed namespaces:
#   - security:  For security modules (SELinux, AppArmor)
#   - system:    For system purposes (ACLs, capabilities)
#   - trusted:   For privileged operations (root only)
#   - user:      For user applications
#
# User attributes are only supported on regular files and directories
# and require the filesystem to be mounted with user_xattr (for some filesystems
# like ext2/ext3/ext4, though modern kernels often enable it by default).
#
# Reference: attr(5), xattr(7)
# =============================================================================